The '''1998–99 season''' was the 105th season of competitive [[1998–99 in Scottish football|football]] by [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]. Celtic competed in the [[1998–99 Scottish Premier League|Scottish Premier League]], [[1998–99 UEFA Cup|UEFA Cup]], [[1998–99 Scottish League Cup|Scottish League Cup]] and the [[1998–99 Scottish Cup|Scottish Cup]].

As defending league champions, they were now managed by Slovak coach Jozef Venglos following the resignation of Wim Jansen. However, they finished runners-up behind Rangers this season and also lost to them in the Scottish Cup final.

==Summary==
Season 1998–99 saw Celtic finish second in the league six points behind the winners, [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://scottishfootballarchive.co.uk/league-tables/1998-99-premier-league |archive-url=https://archive.today/20130505131120/http://scottishfootballarchive.co.uk/league-tables/1998-99-premier-league |url-status=dead |archive-date=5 May 2013 |title=1998-99 Premier League |publisher=Scottish Football Archive |access-date=5 December 2011 }}</ref> They reached the final of the Scottish Cup losing to [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]],<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/sc/1998-99.html | title=Scottish Cup Results for 1998-99 | publisher=London Hearts | access-date=5 December 2011}}</ref> the third round of the League Cup losing to [[Airdrieonians F.C. (1878)|Airdrieonians]],<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/lc/1998-99.html | title=Scottish League Cup Results for 1998-99 | publisher=London Hearts | access-date=5 December 2011}}</ref> the second qualifying round of the Champions League<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/history/clubs/50050--celtic/ | title=UEFA Champions League 1998/99 Celtic | publisher=Uefa | access-date=5 December 2011}}</ref> and the second round of the UEFA Cup, losing to [[FC Zürich]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/history/clubs/50050--celtic/ | title=Celtic 1998/99 Uefa Cup | publisher=[[UEFA]] | access-date=5 December 2011}}</ref>

